<h1>Sex and marriage</h1>
<h2>October 2, 2026</h2>
I discuss the left-wing media’s attacks in traditional marriage, and
 the “Cornell 7” sex scandal.
<a name="2026-10-02-traditional-wives"> </a>
<h3>Traditional wives</h3>
<p>My first marriage was a traditional marriage: I worked and paid all
 of the bills while my wife took care of our baby. That in mind, I am a
 great supporter of the “Trad wife” lifestyle.
<p>The left wing media doesn’t support this lifestyle: The New York
 Times posted a hit piece about <a href="AI/2026-09-24-AntiTradWifeNYT.html">one former Trad Wife who divorced her husband</a>, 
implying that
 traditional marriages do not work out. New York Magazine went further,
 and used <a href="AI/2026-10-02-AntiTradWifeNymag.html">this New York Times piece and some other examples to make the case traditional marriages can’t  work</a>.
<p>Never mind that, while it was a challenging marriage, I stayed with
 my wife, faithful to her (and, yes, the sex was fantastic) until her
 untimely death from cancer.
<p>We are in a fertility collapse right now. People who follow this
 left-wing agenda promoted by the New York Times and New York Magazine,
 an agenda which discourages conservative traditional families, will
 tend to not have children. People who ignore or fight back against this
 left-wing agenda will have more children, and show their families a
 world view encouraging a traditional marriage where the man brings the
 bacon home while the woman raises the children, leading to there being
 more traditional families.
<a name="2026-10-02-the-cornell-7"> </a>
<h3>The Cornell 7</h3>
<p>I should comment on the Cornell 7 case. For people who haven’t heard
 the news, <a href="AI/2026-09-30-BBCcornell.html">here is a BBC  summary</a> 
and <a href="AI/2026-10-01-Ayers.html">here is a well written summary of the actual legal documents which have been made public</a>. 
The radical left is following their agenda here: Since any sex
 that is consensual goes, they have to pound on the “rape” drum when
 deeply immoral and vile sex like this happens. However, in this case,
 whether or not the actual sex is consensual is a side show.
<p>As someone who has never had sex outside of a lifetime monogamous
 commitment, asking a woman who likes you to not only have sex with you,
 but your friend too, is a vile and immoral act. Having more guys enter
 the scene, even if she consented, is even more disgusting. And sharing
 about it on a group chat is hateful and disrespectful towards women. A
 gentleman never “kisses and tells”—if he does something immoral like
 that, which he shouldn’t, he at least should do it discreetly 1-on-1
 with the lady in question, and have the decency to not tell anyone what
 happened to protect the girl’s honor.
<p>The details of the case are very messy, and “Jane Doe” should had
 shut them down as soon as they talked about perversions such as
 threesomes. Doe just having sex with the guy she liked without other
 men being involved would had been <em>less</em> immoral, but I doubt he
 was on the track to marrying her.
<p>The good news is that it appears Jane Doe is doing OK. If the
 identity which Internet sleuths dug up is really her, not only is she a
 very beautiful woman, she now has a boyfriend who loves him; they post
 pictures together on Instagram and it would seem he took her on a nice
 vacation to Europe. I hope she marries this man, I hope he doesn’t hold
 what happened against her, and I hope till death do they part, making
 beautiful children together.


